WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540 line:17%
A diagnosis tells us something about a child's hearing.

00:00:03.365 --> 00:00:05.720 line:17%
The family tells us what a typical day actually

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.180 line:17%
asks of the child.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.870 line:17%
Suppose a clinician wants to start device training, while

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.550 line:17%
a parent is worried about missed conversation at dinner.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.690 line:17%
Once the parent shares that concern, they can plan

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.850 line:17%
together around a routine the family values.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.130 line:17%
The plan now connects a clinical skill to a

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.210 line:17%
real communication goal.

00:00:24.337 --> 00:00:27.417 line:17%
Watch what happens when the audiologist rehearses a reply

00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:28.777 line:17%
while the parent is speaking.

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:32.107 line:17%
Attention shifts away before the concern is complete.

00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:36.047 line:17%
Attending means focusing on the speaker, and observing means

00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:38.287 line:17%
noticing cues such as a change in expression.

00:00:39.207 --> 00:00:41.707 line:17%
Empathy is the effort to understand what the experience

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.407 line:17%
feels like from the parent's perspective.

00:00:44.305 --> 00:00:46.807 line:17%
Let the speaker finish and check what you heard.

00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:50.487 line:17%
That extra information can change the plan you build

00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:51.127 line:17%
together.
